L000456	\section{Matching  with  the spurion method}
L000457	\label{app:matching}
L000458	
L000459	
L000460	The LECs entering Eq.~\eqref{eq:LECs} were obtained by matching LEFT correlators onto ChPT ones at the one-loop level, following the spurion method outlined in Refs.~\cite{Descotes-Genon:2005wrq,Cirigliano:2023fnz}. This method consists of promoting the parameters responsible for the chiral symmetry breaking, i.e.,  quark masses and electroweak charges,
L000461	to dynamical fields transforming under SU(3)$_{L}\times$ SU(3)$_{R}$ in such a way that the LEFT Lagrangian preserves the chiral symmetry. Then, following Refs.~\cite{Urech:1994hd,Knecht:1999ag}, it is possible to build a complete basis of effective operators involving leptons, photons, light mesons, and spurion sources up to order $p^{4}$ in the chiral expansion and respecting  chiral symmetry.
L000462	By computing correlators at the one-loop level in both theories, it is then possible to extract the renormalized LECs, which encode the short-distance physics and the nonperturbative matrix elements at a given order.
L000463	
L000464	These correlators are defined by taking the functional derivatives of the generating functional of the connected diagrams ($W$) with respect to the spurion sources and computing matrix elements between lepton and pion external states as
L000465	\begin{equation}
L000466	    \int d^{4}x\,\bigg\langle l(p)\bar{\nu}(q) \bigg| \frac{\delta^{2} W(\mathbf{q}_{A},\mathbf{q}_{V},\mathbf{q}_{W})}{\delta\mathbf{q}^{b}_{V(A)}(x)\delta\mathbf{q}_{W}^{c}(0)}\bigg|\pi^{c}(r)\bigg\rangle,
L000467	\end{equation}
L000468	where $\mathbf{q}_{V(A)}$ are the spurion sources associated with the vector and axial-vector electric charge, while $\mathbf{q}_{W}$ is the spurion field associated with the weak current, both expressed in the adjoint representation of SU(3). We adopt the LECs basis proposed in Ref.~\cite{Descotes-Genon:2005wrq}, which allows one to separate the electroweak contribution ($\hat{X}_{6}$) from the strong interaction one ($\hat{X}_{1}$, $\hat{X}_{2}$) in the charged lepton kinetic term ($X_{6}$) as
L000469	\begin{equation}
L000470	    X_{6} = \hat{X}_{6} + \frac{4}{3} \hat{X}_{1}+4\hat{X}_{2}.
L000471	\end{equation}
L000472	By adapting the results of Refs.~\cite{Descotes-Genon:2005wrq,Moussallam:1997xx} to the $\overline{\text{MS}}$ (LEFT) and  $\overline{\text{MS}}_\chi$ (ChPT) schemes, respectively, we find:
L000473	\begin{align}
L000474	\label{eq:LECs_separate}
L000475	    \hat{X}_{6} &= \frac{1}{16 \pi^2}\bigg(1- \log\frac{\mu^{2}_{\chi}}{\mu^{2}}\bigg),\\
L000476	
L000477	    \hat{X}_{1}+X_{1} &= i\,\frac{3}{4}\int \frac{d^{d}k}{(2 \pi)^{d}} \bigg[ \frac{\Gamma_{VV}(k,r)}{k^{2}}-\frac{1}{k^{2}(k^{2}-\mu_{0}^{2})}\bigg] \nonumber \\
L000478	    &\qquad+ \frac{1}{16\pi^{2}}\bigg[-\frac{3}{4}\log\frac{\mu^{2}}{\mu_{0}^{2}}+\frac{3}{2}B(a)+\frac{33}{8} \notag\\
L000479	    &\qquad+ \frac{\alpha_{s}}{4\pi}\bigg( 3\log\frac{\mu^{2}}{\mu_{0}^{2}}+ \frac{3}{2} B_{s}(a) -3 \bigg)\bigg],\notag\\
L000480	
L000481	    \hat{X}_{2} &= i\, \frac{3}{8} \int \frac{d^{d}k}{(2 \pi)^{d}}\bigg[\Xi(k^2)-\frac{1}{k^2(k^2-\mu_{0}^{2})} \bigg]\nonumber\\
L000482	    &\qquad+\frac{1}{16\pi^{2}}\bigg(-\frac{5}{4}\log\frac{\mu^{2}}{\mu_{0}^{2}}-\frac{7}{8}\log\frac{\mu_{0}^{2}}{\mu_{\chi}^{2}}-\frac{19}{16}\bigg),\notag\\
L000483	
L000484	    K_{12} &= i\, \frac{3}{8} \int \frac{d^{d}k}{(2 \pi)^{d}}\bigg[\Xi(k^2)-\frac{1}{k^2(k^2-\mu_{0}^{2})}\bigg] \nonumber\\
L000485	    &\qquad+\frac{1}{16\pi^{2}}\bigg(-\frac{1}{4}\log\frac{\mu^{2}}{\mu_{0}^{2}}+\frac{1}{8}\log\frac{\mu_{0}^{2}}{\mu_{\chi}^{2}}-\frac{3}{16}\bigg),\notag
L000486	\end{align}
L000487	where $\Xi(k^2) = k^{2}\big[g_{2}(k^2)-g_{1}(k^2)\big] - \big[f_{2}(k^{2})-f_{1}(k^2)\big]$, $f_{i}(k^2)$ and $g_{i}(k^2)$ are hadronic functions defined in Ref.~\cite{Descotes-Genon:2005wrq}, and the correlator $\Gamma_{VV}(k,r)$ is given by
L000488	\begin{align}
L000489	\label{TVV_corr}
L000490	    &\int d^{4}x\, e^{ik\cdot x} \big\langle 0 \big|T\big\{V^{b}_{\mu}(x) V^{c}_{\nu}(0)\big\} \big|\pi^{a}(r)\big\rangle\notag\\
L000491	    &\qquad=i  F_{0} \, \epsilon_{\mu\nu\rho\gamma}\,k^{\rho}r^{\gamma} d^{abc}\, \Gamma_{VV}(k,r),
L000492	\end{align}
L000493	in terms of the pion decay constant in the chiral limit, $F_0$, and the structure constant $d^{abc}$ of the SU(3) generators.
L000494	 We find that the $g_{i}$ and $f_{i}$ terms cancel out in Eq.~\eqref{eq:LECs}, leaving $\Gamma_{VV}$ as the only nonperturbative term.
L000495	In order to use lattice data from Refs.~\cite{Feng:2020zdc,Yoo:2023gln} for the box-diagram term presented in Eq.~\eqref{eq:box1}, we need to relate the pion-to-vacuum amplitude with the pion-to-pion one.
L000496	This can be achieved by
L000497	generalizing
L000498	the \emph{soft-pion theorem}
L000499	\begin{equation}
L000500	    \lim_{p^{\mu}\,\rightarrow \,0} \langle\pi^{a}(p)\beta|O|\alpha\rangle = -\frac{i}{F_{0}}\langle\beta |[Q_{5}^{a},O]|\alpha\rangle,
L000501	\end{equation}
L000502	where $\beta$, $\alpha$ are arbitrary external states,   $Q_{5}^{a}= \int d^{3}x\, A_{0}^{a}(x)$ is the axial charge,
L000503	and $O$ is a local operator,  to the case in which $O$ is replaced by the time-ordered product of
L000504	two operators.
L000505	In this way we
L000506	obtain the relation
L000507	$\Gamma_{VV}=-3/\sqrt{2}\,T_3^\text{\cite{Feng:2020zdc}}$.
L000508	Using this in Eq.~\eqref{eq:LECs_separate} and inserting the relations~\eqref{eq:LECs_separate}  into Eq.~\eqref{eq:LECs}
L000509	we arrive at Eq.~\eqref{eq:final_res0}, with $\bar \Box_\pi^{V}$ given in Eq.~\eqref{eq:box1}.
